        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We&#x27;re used to seeing summations written in compact form using sigma notation.</p>",
            "readable_text": "We're used to seeing summations written in compact form using sigma notation.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, the notation</p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, the notation",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sum_{i=1}^4 (2i-3)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\sum_{i=1}^4 (2i-3)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>represents the sum of the first <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4]</span> terms of the sequence <span class=\"math\">[MATH: a_i = 2i-3.]</span> We evaluate this series as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "represents the sum of the first [MATH: 4] terms of the sequence [MATH: a_i = 2i-3.] We evaluate this series as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2211_(i = 1)^(4)(2i \u2212 3)|= (2(1) \u2212 3) + (2(2) \u2212 3) + (2(3) \u2212 3) + (2(4) \u2212 3); = (\u2212 1) + 1 + 3 + 5; = 8]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \u2211_(i = 1)^(4)(2i \u2212 3)|= (2(1) \u2212 3) + (2(2) \u2212 3) + (2(3) \u2212 3) + (2(4) \u2212 3); = (\u2212 1) + 1 + 3 + 5; = 8]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We have a similar notation that compactly represents products of terms of a sequence. For this, we use the <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\prod]</span> symbol.</p>",
            "readable_text": "We have a similar notation that compactly represents products of terms of a sequence. For this, we use the [MATH: \\prod] symbol.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>For example, let&#x27;s consider the following expression:</p>",
            "readable_text": "For example, let's consider the following expression:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\prod_{i =1}^{4} (2i - 3)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \\prod_{i =1}^{4} (2i - 3)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>This represents the <em>product</em> of the first <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4]</span> terms of the sequence <span class=\"math\">[MATH: a_i = 2i-3.]</span> We evaluate this product as follows:</p>",
            "readable_text": "This represents the product of the first [MATH: 4] terms of the sequence [MATH: a_i = 2i-3.] We evaluate this product as follows:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u220f_(i = 1)^(4)(2i \u2212 3)|= (2(1) \u2212 3) \u22c5 (2(2) \u2212 3) \u22c5 (2(3) \u2212 3) \u22c5 (2(4) \u2212 3) \u22c5; = (\u2212 1) \u22c5 1 \u22c5 3 \u22c5 5; = \u2212 15]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: \u220f_(i = 1)^(4)(2i \u2212 3)|= (2(1) \u2212 3) \u22c5 (2(2) \u2212 3) \u22c5 (2(3) \u2212 3) \u22c5 (2(4) \u2212 3) \u22c5; = (\u2212 1) \u22c5 1 \u22c5 3 \u22c5 5; = \u2212 15]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nWe're used to seeing summations written in compact form using sigma notation.\n\nContent:\nFor example, the notation\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\sum_{i=1}^4 (2i-3)]\n\nContent:\nrepresents the sum of the first [MATH: 4] terms of the sequence [MATH: a_i = 2i-3.] We evaluate this series as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \u2211_(i = 1)^(4)(2i \u2212 3)|= (2(1) \u2212 3) + (2(2) \u2212 3) + (2(3) \u2212 3) + (2(4) \u2212 3); = (\u2212 1) + 1 + 3 + 5; = 8]\n\nContent:\nWe have a similar notation that compactly represents products of terms of a sequence. For this, we use the [MATH: \\prod] symbol.\n\nContent:\nFor example, let's consider the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\prod_{i =1}^{4} (2i - 3)]\n\nContent:\nThis represents the product of the first [MATH: 4] terms of the sequence [MATH: a_i = 2i-3.] We evaluate this product as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \u220f_(i = 1)^(4)(2i \u2212 3)|= (2(1) \u2212 3) \u22c5 (2(2) \u2212 3) \u22c5 (2(3) \u2212 3) \u22c5 (2(4) \u2212 3) \u22c5; = (\u2212 1) \u22c5 1 \u22c5 3 \u22c5 5; = \u2212 15]"
      },
