        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Express <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\displaystyle \\prod_{n = 3}^{m} \\dfrac{n + 1}{n - 1}]</span> as a function of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: m]</span> only.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Express [MATH: \\displaystyle \\prod_{n = 3}^{m} \\dfrac{n + 1}{n - 1}] as a function of [MATH: m] only.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We expand the product by multiplying over the index <span class=\"math\">[MATH: n]</span> from <span class=\"math\">[MATH: n = 3]</span> to <span class=\"math\">[MATH: n = m,]</span> inclusive: \n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u220f_(n = 3)^(m)(n + 1)/(n \u2212 1)|= (3 + 1)/(3 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (4 + 1)/(4 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (5 + 1)/(5 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (6 + 1)/(6 \u2212 1) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (m \u2212 1 + 1)/(m \u2212 1 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (m + 1)/(m \u2212 1); = (4)/(2) \u22c5 (5)/(3) \u22c5 (6)/(4) \u22c5 (7)/(5) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (m)/(m \u2212 2) \u22c5 (m + 1)/(m \u2212 1); = (4)/(2) \u22c5 (5)/(3) \u22c5 (6)/(4) \u22c5 (7)/(5) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (m)/(m \u2212 2) \u22c5 (m + 1)/(m \u2212 1); = (m \u22c5 (m + 1))/(2 \u22c5 3); = (m(m + 1))/(6)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We expand the product by multiplying over the index [MATH: n] from [MATH: n = 3] to [MATH: n = m,] inclusive:\n[MATH: \u220f_(n = 3)^(m)(n + 1)/(n \u2212 1)|= (3 + 1)/(3 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (4 + 1)/(4 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (5 + 1)/(5 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (6 + 1)/(6 \u2212 1) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (m \u2212 1 + 1)/(m \u2212 1 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (m + 1)/(m \u2212 1); = (4)/(2) \u22c5 (5)/(3) \u22c5 (6)/(4) \u22c5 (7)/(5) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (m)/(m \u2212 2) \u22c5 (m + 1)/(m \u2212 1); = (4)/(2) \u22c5 (5)/(3) \u22c5 (6)/(4) \u22c5 (7)/(5) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (m)/(m \u2212 2) \u22c5 (m + 1)/(m \u2212 1); = (m \u22c5 (m + 1))/(2 \u22c5 3); = (m(m + 1))/(6)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nExpress [MATH: \\displaystyle \\prod_{n = 3}^{m} \\dfrac{n + 1}{n - 1}] as a function of [MATH: m] only.\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe expand the product by multiplying over the index [MATH: n] from [MATH: n = 3] to [MATH: n = m,] inclusive:\n[MATH: \u220f_(n = 3)^(m)(n + 1)/(n \u2212 1)|= (3 + 1)/(3 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (4 + 1)/(4 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (5 + 1)/(5 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (6 + 1)/(6 \u2212 1) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (m \u2212 1 + 1)/(m \u2212 1 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (m + 1)/(m \u2212 1); = (4)/(2) \u22c5 (5)/(3) \u22c5 (6)/(4) \u22c5 (7)/(5) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (m)/(m \u2212 2) \u22c5 (m + 1)/(m \u2212 1); = (4)/(2) \u22c5 (5)/(3) \u22c5 (6)/(4) \u22c5 (7)/(5) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (m)/(m \u2212 2) \u22c5 (m + 1)/(m \u2212 1); = (m \u22c5 (m + 1))/(2 \u22c5 3); = (m(m + 1))/(6)]"
      },
