    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nWe're used to seeing summations written in compact form using sigma notation.\n\nContent:\nFor example, the notation\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\sum_{i=1}^4 (2i-3)]\n\nContent:\nrepresents the sum of the first [MATH: 4] terms of the sequence [MATH: a_i = 2i-3.] We evaluate this series as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \u2211_(i = 1)^(4)(2i \u2212 3)|= (2(1) \u2212 3) + (2(2) \u2212 3) + (2(3) \u2212 3) + (2(4) \u2212 3); = (\u2212 1) + 1 + 3 + 5; = 8]\n\nContent:\nWe have a similar notation that compactly represents products of terms of a sequence. For this, we use the [MATH: \\prod] symbol.\n\nContent:\nFor example, let's consider the following expression:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\prod_{i =1}^{4} (2i - 3)]\n\nContent:\nThis represents the product of the first [MATH: 4] terms of the sequence [MATH: a_i = 2i-3.] We evaluate this product as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \u220f_(i = 1)^(4)(2i \u2212 3)|= (2(1) \u2212 3) \u22c5 (2(2) \u2212 3) \u22c5 (2(3) \u2212 3) \u22c5 (2(4) \u2212 3) \u22c5; = (\u2212 1) \u22c5 1 \u22c5 3 \u22c5 5; = \u2212 15]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Evaluating a Product\n\nExample Prompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: \\displaystyle \\prod_{k=1}^{4} \\dfrac{3k - 1}{6k - 1}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe expand the product by multiplying over the index [MATH: k] from [MATH: k = 1] to [MATH: k = 4{:}]\n[MATH: \u220f_(k = 1)^(4)(3k \u2212 1)/(6k \u2212 1)|= (3(1) \u2212 1)/(6(1) \u2212 1) \u22c5 (3(2) \u2212 1)/(6(2) \u2212 1) \u22c5 (3(3) \u2212 1)/(6(3) \u2212 1) \u22c5 (3(4) \u2212 1)/(6(4) \u2212 1); = (2)/(5) \u22c5 (5)/(11) \u22c5 (8)/(17) \u22c5 (11)/(23); = (2)/(5) \u22c5 (5)/(11) \u22c5 (8)/(17) \u22c5 (11)/(23); = (2 \u22c5 8)/(17 \u22c5 23); = (16)/(391)]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: \u220f_(i = 2)^(6)(2i + 1).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 1441]\nb. [MATH: 45045]\nc. [MATH: 720]\nd. [MATH: 61205]\ne. [MATH: 15120]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nEvaluate [MATH: \u220f_(k = 5)^(8)(2k + 1)/(1 \u2212 2k).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 (19)/(9)]\nb. [MATH: (8)/(5)]\nc. [MATH: (15)/(11)]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 (1120)/(113)]\ne. [MATH: (17)/(9)]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Writing a Product Using Product Notation\n\nExample Prompt:\nExpress the following product using product notation:\n\n[MATH: (2 - 3^2) \\cdot (2 - 4^2) \\cdot (2 - 5^2) \\cdot \\: \\ldots \\: \\cdot (2 - 12^2)]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe can collapse the given expression using product notation over the index [MATH: i] from [MATH: i=3] to [MATH: i = 12{:}]\n\n[MATH: (2 \u2212 3^{2}) \u22c5 (2 \u2212 4^{2}) \u22c5 (2 \u2212 5^{2}) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (2 \u2212 12^{2}) = \u220f_(i = 3)^(12)(2 \u2212 i^{2})]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (2 \u22c5 3^{3} \u2212 1) \u22c5 (2 \u22c5 4^{3} \u2212 1) \u22c5 (2 \u22c5 5^{3} \u2212 1) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (2n^{3} \u2212 1) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u220f_(i = 3)^(n)(2n^{3} \u2212 1)]\nb. [MATH: \u220f_(i = 1)^(n)(2i^{3} \u2212 1)]\nc. [MATH: \u220f_(i = 3)^(n)(2i^{3} \u2212 1)]\nd. [MATH: \u220f_(i = 3)^(n)2n^{3}]\ne. [MATH: \u220f_(i = 1)^(n)2i^{3}]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: (1^{2})/(1^{3} \u2212 1) \u22c5 (2^{2})/(2^{3} \u2212 1) \u22c5 (3^{2})/(3^{3} \u2212 1) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (10^{2})/(10^{3} \u2212 1) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u220f_(i = 1)^(100)(i^{2})/(i^{3} \u2212 1)]\nb. [MATH: \u220f_(i = 3)^(1000)(10^{2})/(10^{3} \u2212 1)]\nc. [MATH: \u220f_(i = 3)^(10)(i^{2})/(i^{3} \u2212 1)]\nd. [MATH: \u220f_(i = 1)^(10)(10^{2})/(10^{3} \u2212 1)]\ne. [MATH: \u220f_(i = 1)^(10)(i^{2})/(i^{3} \u2212 1)]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Simplifying a Product\n\nExample Prompt:\nExpress [MATH: \\displaystyle \\prod_{n = 3}^{m} \\dfrac{n + 1}{n - 1}] as a function of [MATH: m] only.\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe expand the product by multiplying over the index [MATH: n] from [MATH: n = 3] to [MATH: n = m,] inclusive:\n[MATH: \u220f_(n = 3)^(m)(n + 1)/(n \u2212 1)|= (3 + 1)/(3 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (4 + 1)/(4 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (5 + 1)/(5 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (6 + 1)/(6 \u2212 1) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (m \u2212 1 + 1)/(m \u2212 1 \u2212 1) \u22c5 (m + 1)/(m \u2212 1); = (4)/(2) \u22c5 (5)/(3) \u22c5 (6)/(4) \u22c5 (7)/(5) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (m)/(m \u2212 2) \u22c5 (m + 1)/(m \u2212 1); = (4)/(2) \u22c5 (5)/(3) \u22c5 (6)/(4) \u22c5 (7)/(5) \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (m)/(m \u2212 2) \u22c5 (m + 1)/(m \u2212 1); = (m \u22c5 (m + 1))/(2 \u22c5 3); = (m(m + 1))/(6)]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: \u220f_(m = 2)^(n \u2212 1)(2m + 2) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 6 \u22c5 7 \u22c5 8 \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 2n]\nb. [MATH: 6 \u22c5 8 \u22c5 10 \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (2n + 2)]\nc. [MATH: 6 \u22c5 8 \u22c5 10 \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 2n]\nd. [MATH: 2 \u22c5 4 \u22c5 6 \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (2n \u2212 2)]\ne. [MATH: 2 \u22c5 3 \u22c5 4 \u22c5 \u2026 \u22c5 (n \u2212 1)]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: \u220f_(r = 2)^(m)((r + 1)r)/(r \u2212 1) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: m!]\nb. [MATH: (m)/(2)]\nc. [MATH: ((m + 1)!)/(2)]\nd. [MATH: (m(m + 1)!)/(2)]\ne. [MATH: (m!)/(2)]"
  }
